    <div class="section-heading">1.0 INTRODUCTION</div>

    <div class="subsection-heading">1.1 Definitions, Background, Purpose and Specifications</div>

    <div class="subsection-heading">1.1.1 Definitions</div>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">The University of Maine System will hereinafter be referred to as the "University." Respondents to the document shall be referred to as "Respondent(s)" or "Respondent."</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">The Respondent to whom the Agreement is awarded shall be referred to as the "Contractor."</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">The University of Maine System and other components of the University shall be referred to as "Multi-Institution."</p>

    <div class="subsection-heading">1.1.2 Background</div>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Established in 1968, the University of Maine System (UMS) unites six distinctive public universities, comprising 10 campuses and numerous centers, in the common purpose of providing quality higher education while delivering on its traditional tripartite mission of teaching, research, and public service.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">A comprehensive public institution of higher education, UMS serves more than <span data-field="student_count">{{ student_count }}</span> students annually and is supported by the efforts of more than <span data-field="faculty_count">{{ faculty_count }}</span> full-time and part-time faculty, more than <span data-field="staff_count">{{ staff_count }}</span> regular full-time and part-time staff, and a complement of part-time temporary (adjunct) faculty.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Reaching more than <span data-field="population_count">{{ population_count }}</span> people annually through educational and cultural offerings, the University of Maine System serves as a vital resource to the state and its alumni population residing within the state; more than <span data-field="alumni_count">{{ alumni_count }}</span> individuals.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">The System consists of six universities: The University of Maine (UMaine) including its regional campus the University of Maine at Machias (UMM); the University of Maine at Augusta (UMA); the University of Maine at Farmington (UMF); the University of Maine at Orono (UMO); the University of Maine at Presque Isle (UMPI); and the University of Southern Maine (USM). The System also includes the University of Maine School of Law and the University of Maine Graduate and Professional Center.</p>

    <div class="subsection-heading">Campus thumbnails</div>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">University of Maine</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Founded in <span data-field="founding_year">{{ founding_year }}</span>, is the state's land grant and sea grant university. As the state's only public research university, UMaine has a statewide mission of teaching, research and economic development, and community service. UMaine is among the most intensive higher education institutions in the Northeast with nearly <span data-field="enrollment_count">{{ enrollment_count }}</span> students and academic programs that attracts students from Maine and <span data-field="other_state_count">{{ other_state_count }}</span>, and more than <span data-field="total_students">{{ total_students }}</span>. It currently enrolls more than <span data-field="current_enrollment">{{ current_enrollment }}</span> undergraduate and graduate students who can directly participate in research, working with world-class scholars. UMaine offers more than <span data-field="degree_count">{{ degree_count }}</span> degree programs through which students can earn graduate certificates, master's, doctoral or professional science master's degrees. The university promotes environmental stewardship, with substantial efforts</p>

    <div class="footer">
        University of Maine System RFP Rev. 07/01/2020 | Page 3 of 22
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <h1 style="font-size: 14pt;">Request for Proposal – Load Frame Purchase</h1>
        <div style="text-align: right;">
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Dated: <span data-field="document_date">{{ document_date }}</span></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="subsection-heading">1.1.3 Purpose</div>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">The University of Maine is seeking responses to provide a <span data-field="load_frame_spec">{{ load_frame_spec }}</span> for use in the Ferland Engineering and Education Center as defined in this document. This document provides instructions for submitting responses, the procedure and criteria by which the Respondent(s) will be selected, and the contractual terms which will govern the relationship between the University and the awarded Respondent(s).</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">This equipment will be housed in the new Ferland Engineering Education and Design Center which will house the Biomedical Engineering Program and Department of Mechanical Engineering, as well as teaching laboratories for Mechanical Engineering Technology Program. It will also provide space for all UMaine engineering majors to complete their senior capstone projects and collaborative learning classrooms that will serve the entire campus. This equipment will play a vital role in the growth of the UMaine student's university experience and the expansion of the UMaine College of Engineering population.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Respondents should review <span data-field="spec_ref">{{ spec_ref }}</span> of this document to see the full Scope of Services/Products required.</p>

    <div class="subsection-heading">1.1.4 Specifications / Scope of Work</div>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">The Load Frame must have the following specifications:</p>

    <div class="list-item">
        <strong>Load Frame:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Force Capacity: <span data-field="load_capacity_1">{{ load_capacity_1 }}</span></li>
            <li>Max Speed: <span data-field="speed_1">{{ speed_1 }}</span></li>
            <li>Tabletop configuration</li>
            <li>Vertical Test Space: <span data-field="space_1">{{ space_1 }}</span></li>
            <li>Voltage: <span data-field="voltage_1">{{ voltage_1 }}</span></li>
            <li>Distance Between Columns minimum: <span data-field="dist_1">{{ dist_1 }}</span></li>
            <li>A computer with 2 Ethernet ports</li>
            <li>Acceptable manufacturer: MTS Criterion Series 40 Electromechanical Universal Test System C43.504; or model with equivalent specifications</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="list-item">
        <strong>Load Cell A:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Force Capacity: <span data-field="load_cell_a_capacity">{{ load_cell_a_capacity }}</span></li>
            <li>Low Profile Design</li>
            <li>TEDS self-identification capabilities</li>
            <li>Load Cell Mounting Thread: M27 x 2 mm</li>
            <li>13-pin JT Connector</li>
            <li>Acceptable manufacturer: MTS model LPS.504; or model with equivalent specifications</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="list-item">
        <strong>Load Cell B:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Force Capacity: <span data-field="load_cell_b_capacity">{{ load_cell_b_capacity }}</span></li>
            <li>Low Profile Design</li>
            <li>TEDS self-identification capabilities</li>
            <li>Load Cell Mounting Thread: M12 x 1.25 mm</li>
            <li>13-pin JT Connector</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="list-item">
        <strong>Acceptable manufacturer:</strong> MTS model LPS.503; or model with equivalent specifications
    </div>

    <div class="list-item">
        <strong>Computer:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>WIN10</li>
            <li>8 GB RAM</li>
            <li>2x500 GB hard drive</li>
            <li>Ethernet card</li>
            <li>23" LCD monitor</li>
            <li>Load Frame software: Ability to design, run, analyze and report on tests, and to store test data. Ability to collect data from one or more channels for extensometers, load cells or high level signals. Ability to convert reports to PDF format.</li>
            <li>Acceptable manufacturer: MTS TestSuite TW Elite w/ Strain option 1 and Reporter Add-in; or model with equivalent specifications</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="list-item">
        <strong>Grips and Fixtures:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Wedge Grip Set: 50 kN, Manual actuation, Temperature rating -130°C to 315°C, mounting: D Clevis</li>
            <li>Acceptable manufacturer: MTS Model AWG504; or model with equivalent specifications</li>
            <li>Wedge Grip Set: (4) Flat, Serrated steel 16in, 50 kN, -130°C to 315°C, specimen range 0-7.9 mm, face size 50 x 25 mm</li>
            <li>Acceptable manufacturer: MTS Advantage; or model with equivalent specifications</li>
            <li>(2) Attachment Kit: D Clevis (1 ½) female to M27x2.0 Load Cell</li>
            <li>Acceptable manufacturer: MTS PN 10024310; or model with equivalent specifications</li>
            <li>Adjustable Spanner Wrench, 0.25 in Pin, 2-4.75 in</li>
            <li>Acceptable manufacturer: MTS PN 10009742; or model with equivalent specifications</li>
            <li>Adjustable Spanner Wrench, Hook, 1.25-3 in</li>
            <li>Acceptable manufacturer: MTS PN 10009742; or model with equivalent specifications</li>
            <li>Axial Extensometer: Gage Length 50.00mm, Travel +/-25.00/5.00 mm, Temperature Range -100°C to +175°C, Strain Range +/-50% / -10%</li>
            <li>Acceptable manufacturer: MTS Model 634.25F; or model with equivalent specifications</li>
            <li>Axial Extensometer: Gage Length 25mm, Travel +/-2.5 to +/-12.5 mm, Temperature Range -100°C to +175°C, Strain Range -10% to +50%</li>
            <li>Acceptable manufacturer: MTS Model 634.12F; or model with equivalent specifications</li>
            <li>Three and Four point bend fixture, 30 kN Static Force, 10 kN Dynamic Force, Lower fixture span 24-152mm, Upper fixture span 24-76 mm, Temperature range -129°C to 149°C, D Clevis mount</li>
            <li>Acceptable manufacturer: MTS Model 642.01A-02; or model with equivalent specifications</li>
            <li>(4) Bend Fixture Roller 0.5in</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

